  },
  "body": "If uv_spawn() fails after uv__handle_init() has been called, the handle remains in loop->handle_queue. This causes bug if the handle is stack-allocated or freed, and a subsequent loop operation like uv_walk() accesses it.\r\n\r\nThis follows the same pattern as uv_tcp_init_ex() which explicitly removes the handle from the queue on error.",
